From 781214decf3bf6f0c033d1ea7dd0706162163dee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:28:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(sim): rapid-in-stock reads the tool's footprint, not
 its centre

Law (d)'s column reading - the lateral rapid's a / mid / b samples and
#96's vertical dive - now asks "in stock and under the surface the
earlier cuts left" at every sample of the tool's footprint disc of
radius r - gouge_tol (centre, 8 at half radius, 16 on the rim; the
disc rapids_radial and hidden_along already read), not at the centre
alone. A dive centred just off the stock outline whose rim meets the
stock, and a re-entry beside an earlier plunge whose far side is
still uncut, are now RapidInStock and block the post. acquit_by_prior
already reads the whole disc and is unchanged.

Pinned by vertical_rapids: a_dive_centred_half_a_radius_off_the_stock_wall_is_a_rapid_in_stock,
a_re_entry_beside_an_earlier_plunge_with_its_far_side_uncut_is_a_rapid_in_stock,
a_lateral_rapid_centred_off_the_stock_wall_with_its_rim_in_stock_is_a_rapid_in_stock
(all fail on main), plus three clean cases (disc clear of the wall,
disc tangent within the gouge tolerance, lateral clear of the wall).

Fixes #106

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
