From 9ad0fb52121b1be6286e7eb7579e4d1a51dfe55a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:39:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(sim): judge each footprint sample at the tip's own
 height

PR #138 review: the footprint samples were judged at the tip plane, as
if every tool were a square end, so a ball or bull diving beside a
wall with its rim lifted clear of the stock was convicted. Each sample
at radius rho is now judged at z_tip + lift(rho) against
surface_before (which caps at the stock top) - 0 for a square end or
inside a bull's flat, the corner arc outside it, rho / tan(half angle)
up a point - from the judged Cutter (Cutter::lift_at). The lift comes
from Cutter::corner_r / tip_angle, not ToolGeom::nose_radius, which is
the turning nose and 0.0 for every mill kind.

Pinned by vertical_rapids:
a_ball_dive_beside_the_wall_with_its_rim_lifted_clear_is_clean,
a_bull_dive_whose_corner_lifts_clear_of_the_wall_is_clean (both fail
on the previous commit), a_ball_dive_whose_lifted_footprint_still_meets_the_stock_is_a_rapid_in_stock,
a_bull_dive_deeper_than_its_corner_lift_is_a_rapid_in_stock.

Fixes #106

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
