From 3db8e8872895051e1dd68d84e0d6c0a3b82b629c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:47:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(sim): footprint rings judged at the inner ring's lift

PR #138 re-review: with samples only at the centre, half radius and
rim, a stock edge falling between the half ring and the rim was judged
by rim samples lifted almost a full corner, so a real dive into the
wall read clean. The footprint is now 8 rings at d k / 8 with 2 k
points each (the rim's 16 scaled by radius), and a sample on ring k is
judged at ring k - 1's lift - the lowest the tool stands over the band
between them. Both the vertical-dive and the sideways readings take
it; the module doc states the remaining bound (one ring spacing d / 8
radially, the chord bulge angularly).

The bull pin at x 41.6 to Z 24.5 asserted a gouge and is flipped to a
conviction (a_bull_dive_whose_corner_band_meets_the_wall_is_a_rapid_in_stock);
new pins a_ball_dive_with_the_wall_between_its_sample_rings_is_a_rapid_in_stock
(ball 41.51 -> 22.5 and 42.0 -> 24.0) and
a_bull_dive_whose_flat_reaches_over_the_wall_is_a_rapid_in_stock
(bull 42.2 -> 24.5) - all three fail on the previous commit; the ball
42.9 -> 24.5 stays clean.

Fixes #106

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
